WEBVTT

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:09.190
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.530
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.240
but also in crime.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.490
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:19.910
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.080
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:49.230
moshimo ima anata no yume no eria ga
Should the area of your dreams

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:53.990
namida ni okasare
Be invaded now by tears

00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:01.330
kujiketa toki wa nee kokoro de
When I faltered, in my heart

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:07.960
watashi no namae yonde
My name calls

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:12.210
hurry up hurry up ai no tsubasa
Hurry up, hurry up, the wings of love

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:19.720
anata no sora e tonde yuku
Will fly to your sky

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:24.060
I’m gonna fly fly away

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:27.060
KONDISHON GUURIN
Condition green

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:33.150
mukai kanashimi wo tasuketai no
Do you want to help this deep sorrow?

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:36.150
Just fly fly away

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:42.370
onaji itami wo mune no REDAA wa
The radar of your heart

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:47.790
itsu demo kanjite iru wa
Is always feeling the same pain

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.130
Just I'm gonna fly away

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:31.080
I hope you're ready.
There's no turning back now.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:36.420
Well, then, go to it.

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:46.560
It's Plessie.

00:02:49.310 --> 00:02:53.310
Orders of the Coast Guard

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:56.820
It happened last night around 10 p.m.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:01.570
A report came in that something
was happening out at the shrine.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.870
I saw it! I saw it, I tell you!

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:11.290
Hold on, Katsuji. Wait your turn!

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.790
I gathered some young
men and initiated a search.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:17.500
I saw it!

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.300
Be quiet!

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.590
What did you see?

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:22.380
I...

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.600
We found this man, and
saved him from drowning.

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:26.720
Drowning?

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.680
I saw it!

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:29.850
Saw what?

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:31.270
I saw it...

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:32.100
Katsuji!

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:37.270
I've told you not to go
so close to the shrine.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.400
You dropped lobster
traps there, didn't you?

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:42.240
I saw it!

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:45.620
Naturally. Plessie's nest
is near the shrine.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:46.490
Plessie?

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:47.990
Mmm.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.960
I'm speaking of a
long-necked reptile.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:56.880
Its fossil record spans the
late Mesozoic to the mid-Jurassic.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:00.710
Rumor says one
lives in Loch Ness, too.

00:04:00.710 --> 00:04:03.260
You can't mean... a plesiosaurus!

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:03.930
Yep.

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.390
Maybe you saw a shark,
and made a mistake.

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.680
I'm a fisherman. I don't
make that kind of mistake.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:14.980
But if you have...

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:17.310
why isn't your town world famous?

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:22.820
The entire village has been
working to avoid that fame.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:23.610
Why?

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:29.160
The scientists would ruin
our fishing grounds. We'd starve.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:31.700
You idiot!

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.790
Thanks to you, all our hard
work is completely ruined!

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:36.080
What should we do?

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:39.670
We're under the coast guard's jurisdiction.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.460
Then let's do it!

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:44.510
Well, all right.
Call Ota and the others.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:45.630
Yes, sir!

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.640
All right!

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:55.480
Stop!

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:57.730
It's too narrow, Hiromi.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.690
What's going on up here?

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:04.860
I'm sorry. A tighter turn
would hit the mountainside.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.490
But your wheel is
going over the edge.

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:09.660
Shinshi, raise the
deck for machine 2.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.160
How come?

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:14.120
If the carriers can't take
us in, we'll have to walk.

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.830
Oh, that's right...

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:20.500
Try using your brain the
next time you face the unexpected.

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:24.010
And here he is: Officer Ota,
the master of improvisation!

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.340
Hello, viewers.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:33.640
This is Special Vehicles,
Second Section,

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.100
the Gargoyles of the Capitol.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:39.560
Behind them is a trail of crying
babies and toppled tombstones.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:44.780
Ahead of them lies a
penniless fishing village.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.290
Ha. I won.

00:06:01.420 --> 00:06:06.300
The unrivaled Second Section!
Who will be their next victim?

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:26.110
Might as well be comfortable,
if you're standing guard.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:29.990
The rest of your team is
enjoying themselves. Here.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:30.820
Thanks.

00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:39.160
Shikura Village Men's League
Plessie Protection Committee.

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:42.170
You seem rather well prepared.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.090
That's so.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:46.920
Is that so?

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.800
Yep. That's so.

00:06:59.390 --> 00:07:01.310
How about this one?

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:04.310
Yeah, a perfect impression.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:08.780
What are they doing?

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:12.280
They're taking a souvenir footprint.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:14.530
A souvenir?

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:16.080
Yep. That's so.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:21.710
Whatever.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.430
Here, have a drink.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:35.140
I'm sorry, but we're on duty.

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:37.180
That was then, this is now.

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:39.350
Your captain's asleep.

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:41.310
We really can't.

00:07:41.310 --> 00:07:42.350
Please.

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:45.480
Please.

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:00.700
We really appreciate the show.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:04.670
It's nothing. Just leftover
stock from last year.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:08.550
Should we be doing this?

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:09.170
Why not?

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:13.180
Those reporters are
right around the corner.

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:16.600
They're just waiting
for action, too.

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:21.140
Besides, they'd rather
report on Plessie than us.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:23.850
Ingram vs. Dinosaur?

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:25.100
Ah.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:28.860
Don't kill Plessie.

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:29.820
What?

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:33.570
If you do catch her,
don't you dare hurt her!

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:42.700
It's a miracle she managed to
survive so many billions of years.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:46.710
Please be gentle with her.

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:52.970
We promise, sir.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:15.740
Look at this!

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:17.660
The new hot spot
is Shikurahama Bay!

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:20.660
Everyone wants to see
the battle of the century,

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:25.160
as that scientific wonder,
the mighty police Ingram,

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:29.040
battles a prehistoric monster
shrouded in mystery!

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.960
Who will win? The Ingram?
Plessie?

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:35.300
Send your votes
to your local station!

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:40.430
What's going on here?

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:43.270
I guess nobody has
anything better to do.

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:48.060
No, don't rub those grubby
hands on my Alphonse!

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.440
Oh, no, too late!

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:54.900
I understand the excitement.
I would have come to see, too.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.160
They have no idea of
the danger they're facing!

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.700
Please keep your distance!
The reef is dangerous!

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:04.540
That's where Plessie's nest is!

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:11.250
If Plessie is real, this crowd's
going to be quite a problem.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:13.710
Miss Izumi,

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:18.800
I think we should
recharge Alphonse soon.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:22.680
What? You're going to bring the
carrier through that traffic jam?

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:25.390
That would be one
sweet piece of driving.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:29.100
If I start walking, they'll
have to get out of my way.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:30.480
Ota!

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:34.570
That attitude is what keeps
our accident rate so high.

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:36.530
Yes, right...

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:42.070
Okay, I'll walk to the carrier
if you save my spot, Asuma!

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:42.620
Your spot?

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:44.830
This stretch of beach
where Alphonse is standing.

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:47.540
All right...

00:10:49.790 --> 00:10:53.540
Reserved for
Special Vehicles,
Second Section

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:02.300
Excuse me...

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:04.180
Okay.

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:07.640
Thank you!

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:08.180
Sure...

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:11.350
Officer Asuma, after
machine one is charged,

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:14.400
could you save our space, too?

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.860
Where did the captain go?

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:19.990
He said he had to talk
to the prefecture police.

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:22.610
He gets all the luck.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:38.920
They certainly look healthy.

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:45.800
Anyway, since nothing's happening,

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:48.390
they're going to pull
us out tomorrow.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:56.400
I see. What if Plessie comes
ashore to terrorize the tourists?

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:03.280
I saw it!

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:07.990
Thanks.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:11.750
Then it's the Coast Guard's problem.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:13.420
Is that so?

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:14.540
Yes, that's so.

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:19.420
Are we pulling out?

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:24.510
They're so well prepared
here, I'm sure they can handle it.

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:28.600
Here.
I don't think it's poisoned.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:53.040
We can't let the Patlabors leave.

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:58.040
If the Patlabors stay,
the TV crews stay.

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:05.010
The only thing useful we
ever catch in August is jellyfish.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:09.050
Our dreams of
development have vanished,

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:11.560
along with all the young women.

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:13.180
Our nation has forsaken us!

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:16.600
We have to do whatever
we can to restore this village!

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:19.650
We tried hot springs.

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:22.110
We salted the beach with gold dust.

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:26.070
We became sister city to Jakarta.

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:30.660
And every scheme ended in failure.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:35.330
Our treasury is empty.
It's time to end this losing streak!

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:40.420
We need a home run hit
that will blow away our bad luck!

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:46.550
Plessie is our trump card.
This is going to save our village!

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:51.720
But, sir, Plessie's
still a bit too much for us.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:54.930
We need more time.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:14:01.360
We've run out of time, the
Patlabors leave in the morning.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:02.520
But...

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:07.990
The people on shore need
something to stir them up.

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:16.040
Something doesn't feel right.

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:18.920
There are too many
tourists, but that's typical.

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:21.380
Isn't it a bit overblown?

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:25.590
The TV stage, the advertisements,
all the arrangements?

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:29.300
You know, the captain said
much the same thing.

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:37.980
Let's go for a walk.

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:40.440
Me?

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:43.770
Sure. Yamazaki, you too.

00:14:52.160 --> 00:14:53.410
Captain!

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:56.490
This is a pretty narrow
path for a nighttime walk.

00:14:56.950 --> 00:14:58.460
Don't worry.

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:09.050
I don't know what
you're thinking about,

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:11.550
but are you sure we're
the right ones for this job?

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:14.100
You scared?

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:17.770
Captain!

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:21.810
What's going on?

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:40.960
Hurry up! The tail is
already in the water!

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:51.340
Hold on, I may have an operating
license, but it only covers farming Labors.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:53.930
Same as Katsuji, and
he's already out there.

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:58.220
I wanted to get a haircut
before the TV crews arrived.

00:15:58.220 --> 00:15:59.390
What's taking you so long?

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:03.310
You might think of paying me.

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:05.810
Good evening, we found you.

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:27.290
Miss Kumagami, it's a hoax.
It's all fake!

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:31.760
Step away! We are
impounding this as evidence!

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:37.180
Stand back! Move away
from the equipment!

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:41.100
What's that?

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:41.980
Look!

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:58.910
Momoko, hurry! It's here!

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:00.580
It is? Really?

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:04.290
Hooray!

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:11.960
What's that?

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:13.470
Something's strange.

00:17:16.380 --> 00:17:19.640
I saw it, and now
everyone else will, too!

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:26.440
Do you see that? It's Plessie!
That's the tail of a plesiosaurus!

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:30.900
How carefree she seems.
Look, she's raised a fin!

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:34.820
She seems almost happy.
This is incredible!

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:36.570
She almost seems to be waving!

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:39.030
You won't make fools of us!

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:48.880
Hey, maybe I can use
this to get some lobsters!

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:57.430
You coward! Come ashore
and fight fair and square!

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:00.390
Ota, it can't understand you.

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:01.890
Hard at work, I see.

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:05.600
Captain, why are they here?

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:08.560
Tonight they were portraying
the upper half of Plessie.

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:10.770
Then what is that?

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:14.230
Why, that must be the lower half.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.190
It's fake?

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:18.450
Asuma, what a disappointment.

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:21.070
The eyes of the world are upon us.

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:25.620
The quicker we wrap this up,
the quicker we can take our vacation.

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:27.410
Vacation?

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:33.000
I called HQ from the police
station, and they confirmed it.

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:37.340
Noa, let's go!

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:39.340
You mercenary.

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:46.020
Plessie has been revealed
as a submersible Labor!

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:52.980
Special Vehicles is moving
to attack the fake Plessie.

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:56.320
Good luck, Special Vehicles!
Good luck, Plessie!

00:18:57.190 --> 00:19:00.950
Oh, which side should I root for?

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:03.870
I'm detecting engine noise...

00:19:03.870 --> 00:19:04.950
It's definitely a Labor.

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:09.330
Officer Ota, you only have
one net, so aim carefully.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:13.330
Understood. Leave it to me.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:24.850
He got him! Pull, Noa!

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:29.430
What was that?

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:34.270
I saw it! I really did! Oops, I guess
this isn't the time for that.

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:37.610
Now that's a big catch!

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:39.740
Should I try this? Or this?

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:51.080
So finally, Plessie's true
form is revealed!

00:19:57.550 --> 00:20:00.130
Oh, no, it broke.

00:20:00.130 --> 00:20:03.010
What are you doing, Ota?

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:06.600
What? Why weren't
you backing me up?

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:09.560
You're blaming me?

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:10.730
He's getting away!

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:15.440
Not for long!

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:23.200
Submit, criminal!

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:26.660
Ota, don't!

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:37.880
Oh, how pretty!

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:40.090
Like fireworks.

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:40.800
Momoko...

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:42.590
As expected,

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:46.550
incident 18, in Division 2's
litany of reckless destruction!

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:51.390
I think it was a mistake
to ask for the Labor unit.

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:54.020
The Gargoyles of the Capitol.

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:55.980
They scare me.

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:56.730
Me too.

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:09.200
Want some?

00:21:10.410 --> 00:21:11.080
No.

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:13.000
Here it comes!

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:44.940
What's wrong, Noa?

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:50.830
Everyone's gone.

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:52.700
It figures.

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:56.660
Naturally, once they
found out about the hoax.

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:02.250
Excuse me, are you the Labor team?

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:12.220
Thank heavens! Look, Hiroyuki,
these people run the Ingrams.

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:19.690
He's a big fan of yours.
He especially likes the Labor carrier.

00:22:20.860 --> 00:22:23.320
Ingram! Ingram!

00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:27.820
If you don't mind, could
we have a picture with you?

00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:30.780
Sure.

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:37.120
Everybody smile!

00:23:00.810 --> 00:23:04.820
arashi ga itsushika owatta
When I looked out, the storm had passed a long time ago.

00:23:06.900 --> 00:23:12.570
yuube no kobushi wa kirei ni
The morning dew betrays how yesterday's...

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:14.530
arawareta
sorrows have been washed away.

00:23:15.790 --> 00:23:20.000
yoake ga NEJI wo yurumereba
Dawn is let loose by unbolting the panels of night.

00:23:21.870 --> 00:23:28.300
MASHIN ya BIRU ga mezameru
Even machines and the buildings all wake up.

00:23:29.090 --> 00:23:30.550
I got it

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:38.100
tooku ga mieru yo PANORAMA mitai sa
Now I can see so far ahead, an unfolding panorama.

00:23:38.270 --> 00:23:43.980
doko kara mite mo heiwa-na Happy Island
Wherever I watch from, I see a peaceful, happy island.

00:23:44.110 --> 00:23:45.520
One more chance

00:23:45.730 --> 00:23:53.160
kimi ni oshietai kimi ni tsutaetai
The thing I want to tell to you, the thing I want to show to you

00:23:53.280 --> 00:23:58.620
yume no GEITO ga me no mae de
The shining gate to our dreams lays open to us...

00:23:59.330 --> 00:24:02.290
ima hiraku yo
right now before our eyes.

00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:11.800
This story is fiction...

00:24:07.800 --> 00:24:11.800
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:16.720 --> 00:24:23.270
Haneda New Sky Hotel!
Isn't the south view of the hotel great?

00:24:23.270 --> 00:24:25.810
If I didn't have to work here,
I would enjoy it a lot more.

00:24:25.810 --> 00:24:29.360
Some terrorists planned to bomb
the hotel's tower.

00:24:29.360 --> 00:24:31.240
Luckily, the bomb exploded
in their possession,

00:24:31.240 --> 00:24:33.200
and funny enough, they got stuck,
and couldn't get down.

00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:36.070
Hey! That's so wrong!
You have to aid in their rescue, Asuma.

00:24:36.070 --> 00:24:39.660
Next episode: Save the Terrorists.
Target, locked on!

00:24:38.870 --> 00:24:43.920
Next episode

00:24:38.870 --> 00:24:43.920
Save the Terrorists
